    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190030": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Family Medicine Location: Remote Work - New York The Department of Family Medicine is seeking a Family Medicine Physician faculty member to work within Highland Family Medicine where there are ample opportunities for faculty development within a robust tradition of mentorship. Teaching and clinical supervision of family medicine residents and fellows, medical students and other trainees is an integral part of this position. Duties may at times include any combination of the following:  Patient care, teaching, independent or sponsored research, administrative duties, community outreach, and University-related public service.  The exact distribution of these responsibilities will vary from time to time according to University, department, and division needs, your interests, and your career trajectory.  In general, this applicant will be expected to be a productive member of the University community, whether productivity is measured by patient care, active research, teaching, and/or administrative service. Qualifications: •    M.D./ D.O. Degree or equivalent •    Eligible for a New York State Medical License •    Experience in an outpatient setting is required •    Must meet all credentialing requirements •    Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required •    Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account.  For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Taylor Alvarado at taylor_alvarado@urmc.rochester.edu. The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192455": {
      "title": "Vice Chair, Department of Family Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Family Medicine Location: Highland Family Medicine  The University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry (URSMD) Department of Family Medicine (DFM) is one of the original academic Family Medicine departments in the country.  The Department continues to lead primary care in the 21st century with notable strengths in the bio-psychosocial model, women’s health, global health, and caring for underserved populations. The Highland Family Medicine practice, representing 24,000 patients over 75,000 annual visits, provides access and high-quality care with interprofessional teams. The department is known for its commitment to interprofessional practice and education. DFM educational programs include a nationally known Family Medicine Residency program and three Family Medicine fellowship programs (Maternal child/Advanced Obstetrics, Faculty Development, and Sports Medicine). Besides FM fellows and residents, the department trains other learners including URSMD medical students, Marriage and Family Therapy Interns, Post Master’s Nurse practitioners, and Pharmacy students and residents. As an academic department of the University of Rochester School of Medicine, DFM is led by Colleen T. Fogarty. MD, MSc, the William Rocktaschel Professor and Chair. The Vice Chair is a faculty member of the DFM, who works closely with the Chair as a member of the senior leadership team. In this role, the Vice Chair reports to the Department Chair. The Vice Chair is responsible for ensuring faculty success in clinical care, education, research and scholarship through provision of leadership in faculty onboarding, assignment of mentors, annual review, promotion and tenure processes, faculty development planning, and periodic departmental review of faculty success and needs. Essential Responsibilities: Provides leadership, oversight, and consultation to the DFM Chair about faculty needs and function across the clinical, academic and education missions. Support individual faculty success and scholarship. Collaborate with the URSMD Office of Academic Affairs to oversee DFM faculty appointments and promotions. Collaborate with the Chair on shaping policy and DFM leadership decisions and process. Foster and model a commitment to a culture of support and high standards, identifying strengths and responding to needs of individual faculty members, with attention to alignment with DFM and wider University of Rochester Medicine missions. Work with Residency leadership to engage residents who wish to consider future practice in academic Family Medicine. About the University of Rochester Medical Center: The University of Rochester Medical Center (URMC) is one of the nation's leading academic medical centers, dedicated to advancing health through research, education, and patient care. As a major employer in the Rochester region, URMC encompasses the School of Medicine and Dentistry, Strong Memorial Hospital, Golisano Children's Hospital, and a regional network of community hospitals and outpatient facilities. Our mission is to improve the health of the communities we serve by providing compassionate, high-quality care, conducting groundbreaking research, and educating the next generation of healthcare professionals. MD or DO degree or equivalent from an accredited institution. Board Certification in Family Medicine. Eligibility for an unrestricted medical license in New York State. Demonstrated record of progressive leadership experience in an academic medical center or large healthcare system. Evidence of proficiency in clinical practice, medical education, research, and scholarship. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Commitment to advancing the department's culture and strategic priorities by fostering a respectful, collaborative environment that supports high-quality care for all patients and educational excellence for all learners. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Taylor Alvarado at taylor_alvarado@urmc.rochester.edu. The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181230": {
      "title": "Emergency Physician (SMH + Regional B)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Emergency Medicine Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The University of Rochester, Department of Emergency Medicine seeks committed physician faculty members to teach and practice at Strong Memorial Hospital, Strong West and other Regional Hospitals which are a part of the University of Rochester, a tertiary care teaching facility located in Rochester, NY. Salary is dependent on experience. Candidates must be Board certified (or Board eligible) in Emergency Medicine. Clinical responsibilities include patient care and teaching of house staff and medical students. Participate in monthly division meetings, administrative functions and institutional committees as requested. Your employment is contingent upon satisfactory completion of a health screening exam, pre-placement TB test and your full cooperation in completing screening for the illegal use of drugs. The University of Rochester is responsive to the needs of dual career couples. EOE Minorities/Females/Protected Veterans/Disabled Candidates must be Board certified (or Board eligible) in Emergency Medicine and have a NYS Medical License If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Andrea_DAngelo@URMC.rochester.edu. The referenced pay range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job's salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
