    "https://apply.interfolio.com/143934": {
      "title": "Radiologist - Division Head - Abdominal Radiology",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Imaging Sciences Location: University of Rochester Medical Center The University of Rochester Medicine’s Department of Imaging Sciences is seeking a Section Head of Abdomen Imaging to oversee a team of 14 faculty members supported by licensed professional extenders and a dedicated radiology communication center. Abdominal imaging faculty perform CT/MRI/US/Abdominal Fluoroscopy, and PET/CT with internal sub-specialization in line with a faculty member interest. We provide diagnostic imaging and teaching at the primary medical center and collaborate with superb clinical colleagues. Biopsies and other invasive procedures are performed by a separate interventional division. Overnight coverage is provided by a separate emergency radiology division. Role Benefits Professional activities are supported by a generous individually managed professional account. The department has maintained an average of one day per week of dedicated academic time to allow for professional development. Section heads get an additional one day every two weeks of protected time and are eligible for a leadership incentive of up to $30,000. Company Benefits Compensation and benefit packages are highly competitive, including 403b and 457 plans, disability insurance, and tuition benefits. As a non-profit institution, service time may count toward the public service federal loan forgiveness program. Faculty enjoy competitive combined vacation and conference time each year. Department of Imaging Sciences The Department of Imaging Sciences at URochester Medicine is a practice of approximately 145 radiologists and 50-60 residents and fellows. Technical highlights include state of the art information technology, 3T MRI, a clinical PET/MRI, Dual Energy CT and digital PET/CT. The department's PACS system is integrated into a comprehensive electronic clin