    "https://apply.interfolio.com/163861": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical- UGCA",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: 777 Canal View Boulevard Suite 400 The University of Rochester Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is recruiting for an Assistant Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology at University Childbirth Gynecology Associates. Activities will be primarily based at Highland Hospital, and its outpatient Ob/Gyn practices. The responsibilities of this position will include a combination of clinical and teaching activities, providing obstetric patient care on labor and delivery at Highland Hospital, providing gynecologic care for inpatients, surgical patients and emergency room patients at Highland Hospital, providing outpatient obstetric and gynecologic care at 777 Canal View, and providing call in the hospital in regular and equitable rotation with the other general obstetricians based at Highland Hospital. This call includes supervision of fellows, residents and medical students in the above clinical activities. Qualifications · M.D./ D.O. Degree or equivalent · Eligible for a New York State Medical License · Must meet all credentialing requirements · Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required · Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account.  For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Christine Lee at Christine_Lee@urmc.rochester.edu . The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/164860": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/ Associate Professor/ Professor- REI",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Rochester - NY The University of Rochester Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is recruiting for Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/ Professor in the Division of Reproductive Endocrinology. The Division has an active and growing clinical program with a strong academic portfolio as well as an ACGME approved fellowship in Reproductive Endocrinology. The responsibilities of this position will include: • Clinical duties in the Reproductive Endocrine clinic including competency in Pelvic ultrasound performance and interpretation, Hysterosalpingogram completion and interpretation; • Skill in all clinical aspects of In Vitro Fertilization Treatments; • Competence in basic reproductive surgery and opportunity to work with Minimally Invasive Surgery group depending on the candidate’s interests; • Excellence in teaching skills with the expectation of teaching of medical students, residents and graduate fellows in all areas of Reproductive Endocrinology; • Providing local outreach to General OB/GYN physicians, including participation in local CME and education • Mentoring Residents and Fellows in research projects based in Reproductive Endocrinology; • Providing administrative role in organizing and overseeing the Medical Student Electives in OB/GYN • Option to be involved in national and international research in Reproductive Endocrinology depending on the candidate’s interests Candidate must have an MD or equivalent with board certification or eligibility in Obstetrics and Gynecology and/or subspecialty in Reproductive Endocrinology.  The applicant must be eligible for NYS license.  A post-offer health assessment and drug testing is required to be performed on-site. The University of Rochester has a strong commitment to principles of diversity and, in that spirit, actively encourages applications from groups underrepresented in higher education. · M.D./ D.O. Degree or equivalent · Eligible for a New York State Medical License · Must meet all credentialing requirements · Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required · Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account.  For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Christine Lee at Christine_Lee@urmc.rochester.edu . The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/167116": {
      "title": "REI Division Director- Assistant Professor/ Associate Professor/ Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Rochester - NY The University of Rochester Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is recruiting for an exceptional physician leader (MD, DO, MD/PhD, or DO/PhD) to be the Division Director for Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility (REI). Based on the applicant’s credentials, this appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor/ Associate Professor/ Professor. The Division has an active and growing clinical program with a strong academic portfolio as well as an ACGME approved fellowship in Reproductive Endocrinology. As Division Director, we expect the successful candidate to oversee our internationally recognized program which delivers comprehensive care.  Plans are underway for a new, state-of-the art clinic and IVF laboratory. The clinical care team, composed of 4 faculty members, performs approximately 500 IVF cycles per year and provides the full scope of REI clinical practice services. Additional services include oocyte/embryo cryopreservation, oncofertility, LGBTQ+ family building, recurrent pregnancy loss, preimplantation genetic testing, and men’s fertility. There are numerous academic opportunities at the University of Rochester, including basic, translational & clinical research, supportive research infrastructure, and NIH funded research programs. The responsibilities of this position will include: · Clinical duties in the Reproductive Endocrine clinic including competency in Pelvic ultrasound performance and interpretation, Hysterosalpingogram completion and interpretation; ·  Skill in all clinical aspects of In Vitro Fertilization Treatments; · Competence in basic reproductive surgery and opportunity to work with Minimally Invasive Surgery group depending on the candidate’s interests; · Excellence in teaching skills with the expectation of teaching of medical students, residents and fellows in all areas of Reproductive Endocrinology; · Providing local outreach to General OB/GYN physicians, including participation in local CME and education · Mentoring Residents and Fellows in research projects based in Reproductive Endocrinology; · Involvement in national and international research in Reproductive Endocrinology depending on the candidate’s interests ·    M.D./ D.O. Degree or equivalent ·    Eligible for a New York State Medical License ·    Must meet all credentialing requirements ·    Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required ·    Compliance with University and New York State health requirements ·   Must have subspecialty training in REI and be board certified by the American Board of Obstetrics & Gynecology in REI. ·   The University of Rochester actively encourages applications from groups underrepresented in higher education and medicine. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account.  For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Christine Lee at Christine_Lee@urmc.rochester.edu . The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177942": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Maternal-Fetal Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Rochester - NY The University of Rochester School of Medicine, Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, is recruiting for a full time position (Assistant Professor /Associate Professor/ Professor of Obstetrics and Gynecology appointment based on prior experience) in Maternal-Fetal Medicine. This faculty member will serve with other 8 other full time MFM’s to provide complete maternal-fetal care to those within the Upstate NY region.  Responsibilities including full spectrum perinatal medicine, including L&D coverage and limited in-house night call (approximately 2 per month) as well as home (pager) MFM call.  Faculty are expected to participate in both inpatient and outpatient high risk obstetrical management, ultrasound and ultrasound guided procedures, teaching of fellows, residents and medical students, and research. Candidate must have an MD or equivalent degree with board certification or eligibility in Obstetrics and Gynecology and in Maternal Fetal Medicine.  The applicant must be eligible for NYS license.  A post-offer health assessment and drug testing is required to be performed on-site. The University of Rochester has a strong commitment to principles of diversity and, in that spirit, actively encourages applications from groups underrepresented in higher education. ·        M.D./ D.O. Degree or equivalent ·        Eligible for a New York State Medical License ·        Must meet all credentialing requirements ·        Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required ·        Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account.  For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Anne Hynes at anne_hynes@urmc.rochester.edu . The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179525": {
      "title": "Assistant/ Associate- Midwifery Division",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Rochester, NY  The University of Rochester Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is recruiting for a full-time Midwife at the Assistant/ Associate Faculty level in the Division of Midwifery. The responsibilities of this position will include provision of clinical midwifery services within the framework of an academic medical center. These services include both outpatient and inpatient care of patients of the Midwifery Division, including management of prenatal care, well-woman primary and gynecologic care. - MSN Degree with AMCB Certification in Midwifery - Experience preferred, but new graduates may apply. - Eligible for a New York State Medical License - Must meet all credentialing requirements - Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment  performed on-site required - Compliance with University and New York State health requirements. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account.  For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Christine Lee at Christine_ Lee@urmc.rochester.edu . The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180158": {
      "title": "Assistant Prof/Associate Prof/ Professor (Pelvic Health)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: School of Medicine and Dentistry UR Medicine is dedicated to providing Medicine of the Highest Order through the delivery of innovative, compassionate, patient- and family-centered health care, enriched by education, science, and technology. Our healthcare delivery network is anchored by Strong Memorial Hospital, an 800-bed University-owned teaching hospital which boasts specialty programs that consistently rank among the best in the nation according to US News & World Report. At URMC, our robust teaching and research programs transform the patient experience with fresh ideas and approaches steeped in disciplined science. Here, care is delivered by healthcare professionals who innovate, take intelligent risks, and care deeply about the lives they touch. The University of Rochester Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Division of Urogynecology & Minimally Invasive Gynecology is seeking a full-time fellowship-trained Urogynecologist to join a busy academic clinical practice. The Urogynecology practice offers a full range of services for evaluation & management of pelvic floor disorders within a catchment area encompassing Western New York down to Albany and into northern Pennsylvania. Our blended division allows our Urogynecology faculty to focus on the evaluation & management of pelvic floor disorders and supports collaboration with MIGS faculty for patients with co-existing pelvic pain disorders. Our division works very closely with Colorectal Surgery with a high volume of collaborative surgical cases, as well as with Urology and Plastic Surgery for complex pelvic reconstructions. As faculty, you will receive career mentoring and opportunities to develop an academic career focused on your interests and strengths. Faculty are based at Strong Memorial Hospital with an additional ambulatory surgical center and the clinic site both within a 10 minute drive. Urogyn faculty may expect 2-3 clinic days and 1-3 surgery days per week adjusted for scheduling needs; 1 day of administrative time per week is assigned and adjusted as needed based on administrative roles over time. Strong Memorial Hospital provides a dedicated GYN OR & team for vaginal & laparoscopic cases as well as multiple robotic suites with DaVinci 5 systems. All clinical sites use a common medical record (Epic). Faculty cover after-hours call for the Urogynecology practice and at Strong Memorial Hospital, typically as back-up call for fellows taking first call (gynecology call is covered by the Gynecology & MIGS Divisions). In the clinic, faculty are supported by 2.5 Urogynecology trained APPs, nursing staff who manage clinical triage and acute visits, and office staff. The clinic includes office procedure suites for urodynamics, cystoscopy, intravesical Botox, PNE, & transurethral bulking. The responsibilities of this position will include: · clinical care of patients with complex pelvic floor disorders including surgical and non-surgical management. Proficiency in vaginal & laparoscopic/robotic approaches to pelvic reconstruction is essential. · teaching Urogynecology and Pelvic Reconstructive Surgery Fellows in clinic and the OR, including supervision of after-hours call as scheduled · teaching of other learners including medical students, OB-GYN and Urology Residents in clinic & the OR, as well as Family Medicine & Internal Medicine residents attending clinic for brief clinical exposure experiences · participation in division & department activities including quality improvement, systems improvement, and research activities - M.D./ D.O. Degree or equivalent - Completion of an ACGME-accredited fellowship in Urogynecology & Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery - Eligible for a New York State Medical License - Currently board-certified or eligible for board certification in Obstetrics & Gynecology and in Urogynecology & Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery - Must meet all credentialing requirements - Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required - Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account.  For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Christine Lee at Christine_Lee@urmc.rochester.edu . The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180390": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/ Associate Professor/ Professor- REI",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: School of Medicine and Dentistry The University of Rochester Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is recruiting for Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/ Professor in the Division of Reproductive Endocrinology. The Division has an active and growing clinical program with a strong academic portfolio as well as an ACGME approved fellowship in Reproductive Endocrinology. The responsibilities of this position will include: • Clinical duties in the Reproductive Endocrine clinic including competency in Pelvic ultrasound performance and interpretation, Hysterosalpingogram completion and interpretation; • Skill in all clinical aspects of In Vitro Fertilization Treatments; • Competence in basic reproductive surgery and opportunity to work with Minimally Invasive Surgery group depending on the candidate’s interests; • Excellence in teaching skills with the expectation of teaching of medical students, residents and graduate fellows in all areas of Reproductive Endocrinology; • Providing local outreach to General OB/GYN physicians, including participation in local CME and education • Mentoring Residents and Fellows in research projects based in Reproductive Endocrinology; • Providing administrative role in organizing and overseeing the Medical Student Electives in OB/GYN • Option to be involved in national and international research in Reproductive Endocrinology depending on the candidate’s interests Candidate must have an MD or equivalent with board certification or eligibility in Obstetrics and Gynecology and/or subspecialty in Reproductive Endocrinology.  The applicant must be eligible for NYS license.  A post-offer health assessment and drug testing is required to be performed on-site. The University of Rochester has a strong commitment to principles of diversity and, in that spirit, actively encourages applications from groups underrepresented in higher education. M.D./ D.O. Degree or equivalent Eligible for a New York State Medical License Must meet all credentialing requirements Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account.  For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Christine Lee at Christine_Lee@urmc.rochester.edu. The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180393": {
      "title": "OBGYN Research Associate Chair - Assistant Prof/Associate Prof/Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: School of Medicine and Dentistry The Associate Chair for Research for Obstetrics and Gynecology (OB/GYN) is responsible for leading and coordinating research activities related to women's reproductive health. The Associate Chair for Research will develop and implement research programs, manage research staff, secure funding for research projects, and collaborate with other researchers and healthcare professionals to improve patient outcomes and advance the field of OB/GYN Duties and Responsibilities: Develop and implement research programs: The Associate Chair for Research will work with the OB/GYN department to identify research areas of interest and develop research programs to address these areas. The Associate Chair will also establish research goals and objectives and develop strategies to achieve them. Manage research staff: The Associate Chair for Research will oversee the work of research staff, including graduate students, post-doctoral fellows research assistants, research coordinators, and clinical trainees. The Associate Chair will provide guidance and support to these staff members and ensure that research activities are conducted in compliance with all relevant regulations and guidelines. Secure funding for research projects: The Associate Chair for Research will work to secure funding for research projects through grant applications, fundraising, and other means. The Associate Chair will also develop budgets for research projects and monitor expenses to ensure that projects stay within budget. Collaborate with healthcare professionals: The Associate Chair for Research will work with researchers and healthcare professionals in the OB/GYN department and other departments to develop research projects and collaborate on research activities. The Associate Chair will also work with external partners, such as pharmaceutical companies and other research institutions, to advance research in OB/GYN. Publish research findings: The Associate Chair for Research will publish research findings in peer-reviewed journals and present research findings at conferences and other professional events. The Associate Chair will also ensure that research findings are disseminated to healthcare professionals and the public in a clear and accessible manner. Advanced degree: The Associate Chair for Research should have an advanced degree (PhD or MD) in a relevant field, such as epidemiology, public health, or biostatistics. Research experience: The Associate Chair for Research should have extensive research experience in women's reproductive health, including experience with research design, data analysis, and publication of research findings. Management experience: The Associate Chair for Research should have experience managing research staff and overseeing research projects. Funding experience: The Associate Chair for Research should have experience securing funding for research projects through grant applications, fundraising, or other means. Communication skills: The Associate Chair for Research should have excellent communication skills, including the ability to present research findings to healthcare professionals and the public in a clear and accessible manner. Interpersonal skills: The Associate Chair for Research should have strong interpersonal skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with healthcare professionals, research staff, and external partners. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account.  For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Christine Lee at Christine_Lee@urmc.rochester.edu . The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189539": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate- Faculty Midwife",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: School of Medicine and Dentistry The University of Rochester Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is recruiting for a Fulltime  Midwife at the Assistant/Associate level in the Division of Midwifery. The responsibilities of this position will include provision of clinical midwifery services within the framework of an academic medical center. These services include both outpatient and inpatient care of patients of the Midwifery Division, including management of prenatal care, well-woman primary and gynecologic care. MSN Degree with AMCB Certification in Midwifery Experience preferred, but new graduates may apply. Eligible for a New York State Medical License Must meet all credentialing requirements Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment  performed on-site required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account.  For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Christine Lee at Christine_Lee@urmc.rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process"
