    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191993": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor (UROGYN)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: School of Medicine and Dentistry UR Medicine is dedicated to providing Medicine of the Highest Order through the delivery of innovative, compassionate, patient- and family-centered health care, enriched by education, science, and technology. Our healthcare delivery network is anchored by Strong Memorial Hospital, an 800-bed University-owned teaching hospital which boasts specialty programs that consistently rank among the best in the nation according to US News & World Report. At URMC, our robust teaching and research programs transform the patient experience with fresh ideas and approaches steeped in disciplined science. Here, care is delivered by healthcare professionals who innovate, take intelligent risks, and care deeply about the lives they touch. The University of Rochester Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Division of Urogynecology & Minimally Invasive Gynecology is seeking a full-time fellowship-trained Urogynecologist to join a busy academic clinical practice. The Urogynecology practice offers a full range of services for evaluation & management of pelvic floor disorders within a catchment area encompassing Western New York down to Albany and into northern Pennsylvania. Our blended division allows our Urogynecology faculty to focus on the evaluation & management of pelvic floor disorders and supports collaboration with MIGS faculty for patients with co-existing pelvic pain disorders. Our division works very closely with Colorectal Surgery with a high volume of collaborative surgical cases, as well as with Urology and Plastic Surgery for complex pelvic reconstructions. As faculty, you will receive career mentoring and opportunities to develop an academic career focused on your interests and strengths. Faculty are based at Strong Memorial Hospital with an additional ambulatory surgical center and the clinic site both within a 10 minute drive. Urogyn faculty may expect 2-3 clinic days and 1-3 surgery days per week adjusted for scheduling needs; 1 day of administrative time per week is assigned and adjusted as needed based on administrative roles over time. Strong Memorial Hospital provides a dedicated GYN OR & team for vaginal & laparoscopic cases as well as multiple robotic suites with DaVinci 5 systems. All clinical sites use a common medical record (Epic). Faculty cover after-hours call for the Urogynecology practice and at Strong Memorial Hospital, typically as back-up call for fellows taking first call (gynecology call is covered by the Gynecology & MIGS Divisions). In the clinic, faculty are supported by 2.5 Urogynecology trained APPs, nursing staff who manage clinical triage and acute visits, and office staff. The clinic includes office procedure suites for urodynamics, cystoscopy, intravesical Botox, PNE, & transurethral bulking. The responsibilities of this position will include: -Clinical care of patients with complex pelvic floor disorders including surgical and non-surgical management. Proficiency in vaginal & laparoscopic/robotic approaches to pelvic reconstruction is essential. - Teaching Urogynecology and Pelvic Reconstructive Surgery Fellows in clinic and the OR, including supervision of after-hours call as schedule. -T eaching of other learners including medical students, OB-GYN and Urology Residents in clinic & the OR, as well as Family Medicine & Internal Medicine residents attending clinic for brief clinical exposure experiences - P articipation in division & department activities including quality improvement, systems improvement, and research activities - M.D./ D.O. Degree or equivalent - Completion of an ACGME-accredited fellowship in Urogynecology & Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery - Eligible for a New York State Medical License - Currently board-certified or eligible for board certification in Obstetrics & Gynecology and in Urogynecology & Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery - Must meet all credentialing requirements - Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required - Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account.  For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Christine Lee at Christine_Lee@urmc.rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/145291": {
      "title": "Cornea Ophthalmologist (Assistant Professor - Full Professor)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Ophthalmology Location: Rochester, New York The Flaum Eye Institute at the University of Rochester has openings for full-time Assistant Professor - Full Professor specializing in Cornea. Rank and salary will be commensurate with experience and credentials. Applicants must have graduated from a fully accredited ophthalmology residency and be eligible for licensure in the state of New York. Applicants must have demonstrated a commitment to achieving diversity in the workforce. Candidates must be certified or eligible for certification by the American Board of Ophthalmology The successful candidate(s) will have excellent medical and surgical skills in retina and a commitment to resident and fellow training. Experience in clinical or basic science research is highly desirable. Post-offer health assessment required. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email maria_harisis@urmc.rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/145293": {
      "title": "Pediatric Optometrist",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Ophthalmology Location: Rochester, NY The Flaum Eye Institute at The University of Rochester has an opening for a full - time Pediatric Optometrist at the Flaum Eye Institute’s Comprehensive Eye Care Services and satellite offices. The scope of practice is to provide comprehensive eyecare to children of any age and at times, developmentally delayed adults, including the diagnosis and treatment of eye diseases, aphakic and cosmetic contact lens fittings, myopia management, and co-management of cataract/glaucoma/strabismus with our 4 pediatric ophthalmologists and 2 ocular geneticists. Flaum is a very highly specialized Eye Institute. The Optometrist will be working collaboratively with specialists in pediatric retina, glaucoma, cornea, anterior and posterior segment disease, neuro-ophthalmology, strabismus and all other aspects of pediatric ophthalmology and ocular genetics. There are academic opportunities in teaching, research, and outreach. Teaching will include ophthalmology residents, pediatric and ocular genetics fellows, and medical students. The pediatric optometrist may also have a role in our vision outreach and screening program.  Pediatric low vision skills are a favorable skill for the applicant although not required. The Optometrist can utilize his/her degree to the fullest in our academic environment. Completion of a residency is recommended but not required. Applicants must be eligible for licensure in the state of New York. Candidates must be certified or eligible for certification by the American Board of Optometry. Rank and salary will be commensurate with experience and credentials. Post offer health assessment is required. We look forward to interviewing any interested Optometrist.  Candidates must be certified or eligible for certification by the American Board of Optometry.  Rank and salary will be commensurate with experience and credentials. Post offer health assessment required. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email maria_harisis@urmc.rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/162715": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Research Faculty Position (open rank)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Ophthalmology Location: Rochester - NY The Department of Ophthalmology/Flaum Eye Institute (FEI) at the University of Rochester invites applications for an open-rank, tenure-track faculty position. We welcome candidates with a broad interest in studying ocular structure and function in health and disease. Primary appointment of the new faculty member will reside in the Department of Ophthalmology and Flaum Eye Institute, but there are ready opportunities for secondary appointments in the Center for Visual Science (a university-wide community of >55 faculty engaged in vision research), and other University of Rochester departments (e.g., the Institute of Optics, Neuroscience, Biomedical Engineering, Microbiology and Immunology, Biomedical Genetics, etc.). The faculty hire will have access to considerable shared resources, both within the department of Ophthalmology (shared confocal microscope, histology laboratory, ophthalmic imaging core, biostatistics) and within the Medical Center. The successful candidate will work with an active program of undergraduate and graduate students through multiple, highly-ranked, degree-granting academic programs across the University of Rochester. All candidates should hold a PhD, MD, MD PhD or equivalent. An important expectation for this job position is demonstrated research productivity and the ability to attract extramural funding. Depending on qualifications, an appointment will be made at the assistant, associate or full professor level. Preferred candidates will have expertise in advanced physiological optics (e.g., adaptive optics imaging, optical coherence tomography, scanning laser ophthalmoscopy, two-photon imaging, fluorescence lifetime or other ocular imaging modalities) and/or expertise in advanced cellular and molecular biology, such as single-cell and spatial transcriptomics, proteomics, lipidomics and connectomics, as well as stem cell and organoid approaches for studying retinal physiology. Research areas may involve humans, animal models and/or in vitro systems, as well as computational approaches including machine learning and artificial intelligence. The position will be open until filled, but the application review process will start on July 15 th , 2026. Applications should be submitted on Interfolio (apply.interfolio.com/162715). For questions, email Dr. Ruchira Singh ( Ruchira_Singh@urmc.rochester.edu ) or Dr. Krystel Huxlin ( khuxlin@ur.rochester.edu ). The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/164395": {
      "title": "Optometrist",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Ophthalmology Location: School of Medicine and Dentistry The Flaum Eye Institute (FEI) and the Department of Ophthalmology at The University of Rochester Medical Center in Rochester, New York has an opening for a full-time Optometrist. The position involves working with the Flaum Eye Institute’s Comprehensive Eye Care Services and satellite offices. The scope of practice is to provide comprehensive eye care, including the refraction and dispensing of spectacles and contact lenses, diagnosis and treatment of eye diseases, cataract co-management, and care of dry eyes. We are highly integrated with our Optical Shops and also offer a comprehensive contact lens service including the fitting and management of specialty contact lenses. As FEI is a highly specialized practice, the Optometrist works collaboratively with many subspecialists including the fields of retina, glaucoma, cornea, neuro-ophthalmology, refractive surgery, and pediatric ophthalmology. There are academic opportunities in teaching and research. The Optometrist can utilize his/her degree to the fullest in our academic environment. Completion of a residency is recommended but not required. Applicants must be eligible for licensure in the state of New York. Candidates must be certified or eligible for certification by the American Board of Optometry. Rank and salary will be commensurate with experience and credentials. Post offer health assessment is required. We look forward to interviewing any interested Optometrist.  Candidates must be certified or eligible for certification by the American Board of Optometry.  Rank and salary will be commensurate with experience and credentials. Post offer health assessment required. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email maria_harisis@urmc.rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
