    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194327": {
      "title": "Scientist - Neonatal Lung Biology",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Pediatrics: Pediatrics: Neonatology Location: Rochester - NY The Division of Neonatology in the Department of Pediatrics at the University of Rochester Medicine Golisano Children’s invites applications for a basic science tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor or Associate Professor rank. We seek an outstanding candidate with an PhD degree and postdoctoral research training, with research interests in neonatal lung biology, lung development, pulmonary immunology, or related areas of developmental and translational biology. The successful candidate will establish an independent, externally funded research program focused on understanding mechanisms of lung development, injury, repair, and disease in the developing lung. Candidates whose research complements existing strengths in neonatal lung biology, pulmonary immunology, developmental biology, tissue-resident immune cells, and translational pulmonary research are particularly encouraged to apply. The Division of Neonatology has a strong history of research in lung development and neonatal lung disease and is home to nationally recognized programs in pulmonary biology and developmental research. The University of Rochester is a major site within the LungMAP Consortium, providing opportunities for collaboration with investigators studying lung development, cell biology, immunology, and mechanisms of pulmonary disease across the lifespan. The successful candidate will have opportunities to develop collaborations across the University and with investigators within the LungMAP Consortium and other national research networks. The candidate will be expected to develop an independent research program with strong potential for extramural funding through the NIH and other agencies. The position offers opportunities for collaboration with investigators in Pediatrics, Pulmonary Medicine, Immunology, Microbiology and Immunology, Biomedical Engineering, and other departments across the University of Rochester. The successful applicant will receive a competitive start-up package, dedicated laboratory space, and access to a wide range of state-of-the-art core facilities. The University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry, and adjacent Schools of Arts, Sciences and Engineering provide a highly collaborative research environment with opportunities for cross-disciplinary interactions and collaborations. Candidates must hold a PhD degree and have completed appropriate postdoctoral research training. Candidates should demonstrate a strong record of research productivity and a clear potential to establish an independent, externally funded research program. Research expertise in neonatal lung biology, lung development, pulmonary immunology, developmental biology, tissue-resident immune cells, or related areas is particularly desirable. Candidates with research programs that complement and extend the University of Rochester's strengths in neonatal and pulmonary research are encouraged to apply. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Saabirah_Campo@urmc.rochester.edu. The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176148": {
      "title": "Pediatric Gastroenterologist",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Pediatrics: Pediatrics: Peds Gastro/Hepatology/Nutrit Location: Rochester, NY The Department of Pediatrics and Golisano Children’s Hospital at Strong seek a pediatric gastroenterologist to provide inpatient and outpatient care in their respective clinical settings. We are interested in candidates with pediatric gastroenterology expertise who can assess and treat all pediatric gastroenterology and nutritional disorders. Rotation of call responsibility within the division will also be required. The University of Rochester Department of Pediatrics is nationally/ internationally recognized for its contributions to community pediatrics, pediatric basic and clinical research with global implications for child health, and its outstanding residency program. Minimum Education Requirements: Medical Degree, completion of a pediatric gastroenterology fellowship. Candidates must be BC/BE in pediatrics. Successful candidates will have outstanding clinical accomplishments and a commitment to Pediatric Gastroenterology and Nutrition. Board Certified, NYS, licensed, DEA, fellowship-trained Pediatric Gastroenterologist considered. Candidates must have considerable knowledge and experience in Pediatric Gastroenterology and Nutrition.  All areas of clinical gastroenterology are required. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply for this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns about the position, email Saabirah_campo@urmc.rochester.edu. The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base compensation range for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience, and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/161963": {
      "title": "Clinical Pulmonologist (156088)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Pulmonary Diseases and Critical Care Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Department of Medicine, Pulmonary and Critical Care Division is seeking a full-time faculty position as an Assistant Professor at the University of Rochester Medical Center. The University of Rochester Medical Center (URMC), a leading academic institution, seeks outstanding candidates to join the Division of Pulmonary and Critical Care Medicine (PCCM) in the Clinician-Educator-Scholar Pathway.  The PCCM division comprises 42 full-time faculty members with a wide range of clinical expertise across the pulmonary and critical care spectrum. This position offers a unique opportunity to provide exceptional clinical care, contribute to academic research, and participate in the education and mentorship of trainees in an intellectually stimulating environment. The University of Rochester is a national leader in translational, lung biology, immunology, vaccine development, oncology, and environmental science research. The Department of Medicine and the PCCM division are committed to providing strong and active faculty development programs.  Clinical practice opportunities include providing high-quality, patient-centered care in pulmonary and critical care medicine in the medical intensive care units, pulmonary consultation services, and outpatient pulmonary clinics and performing diagnostic and therapeutic procedures, including bronchoscopy, thoracentesis, and endobronchial ultrasound, as required. Opportunities for basic, clinical, and translational research on lung diseases, including pulmonary fibrosis, pulmonary hypertension, sepsis, asthma, environmental pollutants, and lung cancer screening. We have a competitive T32 funded PCCM fellowship program, and ample opportunities and resources are available to develop careers in medical education. The Rochester area affords the best stress-free living, including affordable housing, easy commutes, highly ranked public schools, and varied cultural, recreational, and outdoor activities. We seek individuals with an M.D. or equivalent and a passion for academic medicine who are board-eligible or board-certified in Pulmonary Diseases and/or Critical Care Medicine and who have completed a three-year fellowship in Pulmonary and Critical Care Medicine to join our diverse and collegial faculty group. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Pulmonary Diseases and/or Critical Care Medicine Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190832": {
      "title": "Clinical Pulmonary & Critical Care Physician (C) (188940)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Pulmonary Diseases and Critical Care Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Department of Medicine, Pulmonary & Critical Care Division is seeking an outstanding candidate with an M.D. or equivalent degree and a passion for academic medicine who are board-eligible or board-certified in Pulmonary Diseases and Critical Care Medicine, to join our diverse and collegial faculty group. The University of Rochester Medical Center is a national leader in translational, lung biology, clinical, and population science research, and maintains a strong and active faculty development program. We have outstanding clinical practice opportunities, including multiple medical intensive care units, inpatient pulmonary disease consultation services, and outpatient pulmonary disease subspecialty clinics (advanced asthma, interstitial lung disease, sarcoid, pulmonary hypertension, pulmonary nodule, thoracic oncology, bronchiectasis, and lung cancer screening). Efforts to support education and basic, clinical, and translational research in lung diseases are available.  We have a competitive PCCM Fellowship Program with 6 fellows per year, supported in part by an NHLBI T32 Training Grant. Our research portfolio is robust and comprises multiple clinical trials, RO-1-funded research in asthma, respiratory failure, lung cancer screening, pulmonary hypertension, and environmental exposures and their impact on respiratory diseases. Many of our faculty are nationally and internationally recognized leaders, including a former president of ATS and leaders in CHEST. The Rochester area offers the best in stress-free living, including affordable housing, easy commutes, highly ranked public schools, and a variety of cultural, recreational, and outdoor activities. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Pulmonary Diseases and/or Critical Care Medicine Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190833": {
      "title": "Interventional Pulmonologist (B) (188941)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Pulmonary Diseases and Critical Care Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Department of Medicine, Pulmonary & Critical Care Division is seeking an Interventional Pulmonologist to join our expanding procedure group (currently 2 Interventional Pulmonologists, 1 advanced bronchoscopist, and advanced practice providers), as part of the larger pulmonary and critical care faculty group.  The division boasts a standalone bronchoscopy suite with anesthesia support at the main campus 5 days per week, with anticipated expansion to regional hospitals.  The pulmonary program at URMC is recognized as a Top Program in Respiratory Disease by US News and World Report, and our cancer center was recently awarded NCI designation. We seek a faculty member with a passion for academic medicine who has completed a three-year fellowship in Pulmonary and Critical Care Medicine and is board-eligible or board-certified in Pulmonary and Critical Care Medicine.  Board certification or eligibility in Interventional Pulmonology is highly desired, but faculty with strong bronchoscopy skills will be considered. Clinical time in the ICU, on Pulmonary Consults, and in the outpatient clinic is available. Protected time for basic, clinical, or translational research can be negotiated. The University of Rochester is a national leader in pulmonary research and maintains a strong and active program in faculty development The Rochester area offers the best in stress-free living, including affordable housing, easy commutes, highly ranked public schools, and a variety of cultural, recreational, and outdoor activities. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Pulmonary Diseases and/or Critical Care Medicine Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190836": {
      "title": "Clinical Pulmonary & Critical Care Physician (A) (188944)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Pulmonary Diseases and Critical Care Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Department of Medicine, Pulmonary & Critical Care Division is seeking an outstanding candidate with an M.D. or equivalent degree and a passion for academic medicine who are board-eligible or board-certified in Pulmonary Diseases and Critical Care Medicine, to join our diverse and collegial faculty group. The University of Rochester Medical Center is a national leader in translational, lung biology, clinical, and population science research, and maintains a strong and active faculty development program. We have outstanding clinical practice opportunities, including multiple medical intensive care units, inpatient pulmonary disease consultation services, and outpatient pulmonary disease subspecialty clinics (advanced asthma, interstitial lung disease, sarcoid, pulmonary hypertension, pulmonary nodule, thoracic oncology, bronchiectasis, and lung cancer screening). Efforts to support education and basic, clinical, and translational research in lung diseases are available.  We have a competitive PCCM Fellowship Program with 6 fellows per year, supported in part by an NHLBI T32 Training Grant. Our research portfolio is robust and comprises multiple clinical trials, RO-1-funded research in asthma, respiratory failure, lung cancer screening, pulmonary hypertension, and environmental exposures and their impact on respiratory diseases. Many of our faculty are nationally and internationally recognized leaders, including a former president of ATS and leaders in CHEST. The Rochester area offers the best in stress-free living, including affordable housing, easy commutes, highly ranked public schools, and a variety of cultural, recreational, and outdoor activities. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Pulmonary Diseases and/or Critical Care Medicine Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
