    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181223": {
      "title": "Faculty - Endocrinology (177583)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Endocrine/Metabolism Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Department of Medicine, Division of Endocrinology and Metabolism at The University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry is seeking a new academic faculty member at the Assistant Professor level, Candidate should be interested in playing a major role in the academic ventures of the division, specifically research, This candidate will be responsible for seeing patients two half days per week and the remainder of the time will be dedicated to research , The Division has tripled in size over the past five years and wishes to continue expansion of all clinical and academic programs, Thus, the University of Rochester offers an exciting opportunity for clinicians interested in academic endocrinology, The University of Rochester has a strong commitment to principles of diversity and, in that spirit, actively encourages applications from groups underrepresented in higher education. Candidates must possess MD degree or equivalent and be eligible for a New York medical license and should have fellowship training in Endocrinology and be board-certified or board eligible in Endocrinology. Post offer Drug Screen, Health Assessment and PPD is required. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Endocrinology Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/159851": {
      "title": "Transplant Hepatologist (153784)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Gastroenterology/Hepatology Location: Rochester, N.Y. The Departments of Medicine and Surgery at the University of Rochester Medical Center (URMC) are jointly recruiting a Transplant Hepatologist to work with our transplant team of  surgeons and partner hepatologists: • Work with the multidisciplinary team to provide patient centered care • Focus on end-stage organ disease management across the entire continuum of patient care, including pre-transplant, transplant, and post-transplant. • Effectively partner with hepatologists and gastroenterologists within the institution and in the region. • Participate in quality improvement processes of the program and work with the team to ensure regulatory compliance Candidates for this position/appointment should be at a level commensurate with promotion to the Associate Professor level. In addition, applicants must be: • Board-certified or Board Eligible in Transplant Hepatology. • Eligible for medical licensure in the State of New York. A generous compensation and benefit package is associated with this position. The University of Rochester Medical Center is an EEO/AA employer. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Internal Medicine, Gastroenterology, Transplant Hepatology Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/159853": {
      "title": "Transplant Hepatologist (153785)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Gastroenterology/Hepatology Location: Rochester, N.Y. The Departments of Medicine and Surgery at the University of Rochester Medical Center (URMC) are jointly recruiting a Transplant Hepatologist to work with our transplant team of  surgeons and partner hepatologists: • Work with the multidisciplinary team to provide patient centered care • Focus on end-stage organ disease management across the entire continuum of patient care, including pre-transplant, transplant, and post-transplant. • Effectively partner with hepatologists and gastroenterologists within the institution and in the region. • Participate in quality improvement processes of the program and work with the team to ensure regulatory compliance Candidates for this position/appointment should be at a level commensurate with promotion to the Associate Professor level. In addition, applicants must be: • Board-certified or Board Eligible in Transplant Hepatology. • Eligible for medical licensure in the State of New York. A generous compensation and benefit package is associated with this position. The University of Rochester Medical Center is an EEO/AA employer. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Internal Medicine, Gastroenterology, Transplant Hepatology Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174393": {
      "title": "Faculty - General Hepatology (169933)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Gastroenterology/Hepatology Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Department of Medicine, Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology is seeking a new faculty member with interest in General Hepatology. Candidates with a special interest and/or expertise in general hepatology, general endoscopy/colonoscopy and digestive health are welcome to apply. The division is the region’s leading tertiary/quaternary level academic GI & hepatology practice with an excellent national reputation, including “high-performing status granted by US News and World Report. The Division enjoys a large robust regional referral practice in hepatology and gastroenterology sub-specialties with investments in industry-leading endoscopic technology and excellent facilities, support and infrastructure. Candidates should have a strong commitment to patient care and teaching. Various clinical research opportunities are available through a well-staffed clinical trials section within the division. Academic rank and salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. The positions offer highly competitive academic institutions. Signing bonus, relocation package, generous vacation and CME benefits are available . M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Gastroenterology & Hepatology Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179615": {
      "title": "Advanced Endoscopy Faculty (175761)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Gastroenterology/Hepatology Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology in the Department of Medicine at the University of Rochester Medical Center is recruiting a new faculty member with interests in Advanced Endoscopy. Candidates with a special interest and/or expertise in General GI, IBD, motility, nutrition and women’s digestive health are also welcome to apply. The division is the region’s leading tertiary/quaternary level academic GI & Hepatology practice with an excellent national reputation, including “high-performing” status granted by US News and World Report. The Division enjoys a large robust regional referral practice in gastroenterology subspecialities with investments in industry-leading endoscopic technology and excellent facilities, support and infrastructure. Candidates should have a strong commitment to patient care and teaching. Various clinical research opportunities are available through a well-staffed clinical trials section within the division. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Gastroenterology and Hepatology Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179619": {
      "title": "Advance Endoscopy Faculty (175763)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Gastroenterology/Hepatology Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology in the Department of Medicine at the University of Rochester Medical Center is recruiting a new faculty member with interests in Advanced Endoscopy. Candidates with a special interest and/or expertise in General GI, IBD, motility, nutrition and women’s digestive health are also welcome to apply. The division is the region’s leading tertiary/quaternary level academic GI & Hepatology practice with an excellent national reputation, including “high-performing” status granted by US News and World Report. The Division enjoys a large robust regional referral practice in gastroenterology subspecialities with investments in industry-leading endoscopic technology and excellent facilities, support and infrastructure. Candidates should have a strong commitment to patient care and teaching. Various clinical research opportunities are available through a well-staffed clinical trials section within the division. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Gastroenterology and Hepatology Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192454": {
      "title": "Infectious Diseases Physician (190692)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Infectious Diseases Location: Highland Hospital The Department of Medicine, Division of Infectious Diseases is seeking an Infectious Diseases Physician at the level of Professor of Clinical Medicine.  Clinical responsibilities include Infectious Diseases consultation and teaching on the inpatient services at Highland Hospital. Responsibilities will also include administrative responsibilities as the Director of Hospital Epidemiology at Highland Hospital. The successful candidate may have opportunities to join established investigative teams working on clinical or epidemiological research, depending on the academic interests of the candidate. Candidates must possess an MD degree or equivalent, be eligible for a New York State medical license, have completed fellowship training in Infectious Diseases and be board-certified or board- eligible in the Infection Diseases specialty.  Post-offer health assessment is also required. The University of Rochester has a strong commitment to the principles of diversity and actively encourages applications from members of groups who are under- represented in higher education. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Infectious Diseases Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176062": {
      "title": "Nephrology Division Chief (171811)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Nephrology Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The University of Rochester Medical Center (URMC), Department of Medicine is seeking a Division Chief for our Nephrology Division. The successful candidate will oversee the growth of the division’s established programs and the expansion and management of the Division of Nephrology. The successful candidate should have leadership experience and be committed to faculty, staff, resident, and fellow education and mentorship.  We seek an academic leader with a track record of leadership in programmatic growth, management, and oversight. URMC is committed to Nephrology. The responsibilities of the incoming Chief will include leadership and oversight of all programs within the Division of Nephrology at URMC and all affiliated hospital sites.  Specifically, the incoming leader will participate in direct patient care and will play a key role in the recruitment and mentorship of all faculty and advanced practice practitioners, as well as the advancement of the clinical, research, and education missions of the URMC Department of Medicine.  The Division Chief will interface with other Divisions in the Department of Medicine, Department of Medicine leadership, Medical School, and health care systems. The Division Chief will oversee and expand active Nephrology services at Strong Memorial Hospital. The Division Chief will oversee and facilitate all career development and educational efforts. Located in Rochester, New York, URMC is one of the nation’s leading academic medical centers. It forms the centerpiece of the University of Rochester’s health research, teaching, and patient care missions. URMC is home to Strong Memorial Hospital, the Eastman Institute for Oral Health, the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry, its faculty practice (University of Rochester Medical Faculty Group), and the University of Rochester School of Nursing.  The University of Rochester’s clinical enterprise, UR Medicine, consists of seven hospitals located throughout the Finger Lakes and Southern Tier regions – Strong Memorial, Highland, F.F. Thompson, Noyes Memorial, Jones Memorial, and St. James hospitals – as well as Golisano Children’s Hospital, James P. Wilmot Cancer Center, Eastman Institute for Oral Health, UR Medicine Home Care, the Highlands at Pittsford and Highlands at Brighton, nine urgent care centers, and an extensive primary care network. UR Medicine’s flagship facility, the 886-bed Strong Memorial Hospital, is designated by the New York State Department of Health as a Level One regional trauma and burn center. The hospital is midway in the development of a new patient tower. This will be the largest capital investment in the University’s history. This will add over 100 ED beds, 48 observation beds, additional CPEP beds (36) as well as 112 in-patient beds with shell space to expand operating rooms.  It is home to nationally renowned clinical care, including Upstate New York’s only cardiac and liver transplant programs, the Del Monte Institute for Neuroscience, Golisano Children’s Hospital, and the Wilmot Cancer Institute, Upstate New York’s premier cancer center providing comprehensive cancer care with expertise in precision medicine, complex cancers, and clinical trials.  With a solid reputation for quality, Strong Memorial Hospital offers some of the top clinical programs in the nation and has earned the National Research Corporation “Consumer Choice Award” all 21 years since the honor’s inception. The Department of Medicine is proud to be the most prominent academic and clinical department at the University of Rochester Medical Center. The Department includes 15 divisions committed to compassionate clinical care, educational excellence, and innovative research.  The team comprises nearly 500 faculty members, over 200 advanced practice providers, 200 residents and fellows, and 800 staff. They conduct around 125,000 outpatient visits per year and 16,000 inpatient discharges.  The faculty includes basic, clinical, and translational scientists researching a broad spectrum of disorders and diseases.  As the largest department, they are dedicated to supporting the community, coordinating community outreach programs, working with affiliate hospitals to ensure quality care is available to all populations across the region, or creating opportunities for youth from all backgrounds to explore careers in health and medicine. On the southern shore of Lake Ontario, Rochester, New York, is just north of the breathtaking Finger Lakes region in Upstate New York. • Stimulating and progressive metropolitan community of 1.1 million people • Stress-free living, including affordable housing, easy commutes, and highly ranked public schools • Cultural district features the Eastman School of Music, The Memorial Art Gallery, and several other museums, theaters, studios, shops, restaurants, and more • More than 100 wineries, breweries, and distilleries • Camping and water sports of all kinds, as well as downhill and cross-country skiing • 6-hour drive to New York City, 3.5 hours to Toronto, and 90 minutes to Niagara Falls and Letchworth State Park — the Grand Canyon of the East Academic rank and salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Board Certification in Nephrology Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193651": {
      "title": "Nephrologist (191987)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Nephrology Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Department of Medicine, Nephrology Division at the University of Rochester School of Medicine is seeking a faculty who has a strong background in clinical nephrology and has a desire to teach and conduct research. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Nephrology Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181229": {
      "title": "Palliative Care Faculty - Asst Prof of Clinical (177589)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Palliative Care Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Department of Medicine, Division of Palliative Care invites applications for a Faculty position within Medicine in the area of Palliative Care. This position will share time between three affiliate hospitals in Dansville (Nicholas Noyes), Wellsville (Jones Memorial) and Hornell (St. James). Duties will include: Patient care, teaching, administrative duties, community outreach, and University-related public service. The exact distribution of these responsibilities will vary from time to time according to University, department, and division needs, your interests, and your career trajectory. In general, this application will be expected to be a productive member of the University community, whether productivity is measured by patient care, teaching, and administrative service . M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Hospice/Palliative Medicine (agreement to become board certified in Internal Medicine and Hospice and Palliative Medicine within two years of hire) Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190139": {
      "title": "Assistant Prof Palliative ED (188174)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Palliative Care Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Department of Medicine, Division of Palliative Care invites applications for a Faculty position within Medicine in the area of Palliative Care. This position will share time between working in an embedded Emergency Department-Palliative Care service and the general inpatient Palliative Care team. Duties will include:  Patient care, teaching, administrative duties, community outreach, and University-related public service.  The exact distribution of these responsibilities will vary from time to time according to University, department, and division needs, your interests, and your career trajectory.  In general, this application will be expected to be a productive member of the University community, whether productivity is measured by patient care, teaching, and administrative service. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Board Certified or Board Eligible in Hospice/Palliative Medicine (agreement to become board certified in Internal Medicine and Hospice and Palliative Medicine within two years of hire) Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192929": {
      "title": "Psychologist to oversee and facilitate addiction treatment",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Psychiatry: Psychiatry: Addiction Psychiatry Location: Strong Recovery The University of Rochester Medical Center (URMC) is actively seeking a doctoral-level psychologist to join the Department of Psychiatry, Addiction Psychiatry Division in a faculty position focused on clinical supervision, workforce development, and federally funded behavioral health research. This role combines direct clinical work, supervision of psychology trainees, program leadership, and participation in clinical trials addressing substance use and co-occurring mental health disorders. The successful candidate will provide supervision and mentorship to psychology residents and postdoctoral associates, contribute to interdisciplinary training programs, and maintain clinical responsibilities within Strong Recovery. A major component of the position involves participation in federally funded research initiatives and randomized controlled trials focused on substance use prevention, digital behavioral health interventions, PTSD treatment, and rural workforce development. Key Responsibilities Include: • Provide individual and group supervision to psychology residents and postdoctoral associates, including direct observation, feedback, and support for clinical competency and professional development. • Maintain clinical responsibilities through psychological assessment services, treatment team participation, coordination of care, and delivery of evidence-based assessment and treatment for individuals with substance use and co-occurring mental health disorders. • Collaborate with Strong Recovery leadership to support program development, training, quality improvement, and the integration of clinical education, research, and innovative service initiatives. • Contribute to initiatives that identify, implement, evaluate, and disseminate evidence-based practices to prevent and reduce substance use and opioid use disorder, particularly in rural communities. • Participate in program development, training, stigma reduction efforts, trauma-informed care initiatives, and evaluation activities that expand access to behavioral health resources and integrated substance use services. • Coordinate clinical activities for a randomized controlled trial evaluating neurofeedback training for PTSD. • Contribute to the implementation of a randomized controlled trial evaluating a digital cognitive behavioral therapy intervention for substance use and co-occurring mental health conditions. • Participate in participant recruitment, screening, enrollment, intervention delivery, and supervision of trainees and research staff involved in study procedures. • Assist with administration and ongoing development of the psychology training program, including recruitment, selection, orientation, evaluation, accreditation activities, and due process procedures. • Coordinate training schedules and educational opportunities, and develop and deliver seminars, didactics, and interdisciplinary educational programming focused on trauma-informed care, collaboration, and evidence-based treatment. The ideal candidate will have experience providing evidence-based assessment, treatment, and supervision for individuals with substance use and co-occurring mental health disorders and a demonstrated ability to work effectively within interdisciplinary clinical, academic, and research settings. Experience in psychology training, behavioral health workforce development, trauma-informed care, and participation in clinical research or randomized controlled trials is highly desirable. As one of the nation's leading academic medical centers, the University of Rochester Medical Center serves as the centerpiece of the University's health research, teaching, patient care, and community outreach missions. URMC's healthcare network is anchored by Strong Memorial Hospital, an 800-bed academic medical center consistently recognized for excellence in patient care, education, and research. The Rochester region offers an exceptional quality of life, combining affordable housing, highly regarded schools, diverse cultural opportunities, and abundant recreational activities. Rochester consistently ranks among the nation's most livable and educated communities. Compensation includes a nationally competitive base salary, comprehensice university benefits, retirement options, annual CME support, tuition benefits, and possible loan forgiveness opportunities. Total anticipated annual compensation by rank: Title                               Range Sr. Instructor                $92,150 - $114,886 Assistant Professor      $101,650 - $136,217 Associate Professor      $129,200 - $177,960 Candidates must hold a PhD or PsyD in Clinical Psychology, Counseling Psychology, Health Psychology, Family Psychology, or a related field from an APA-accredited program. Licensed as a Psychologist in New York State prior to start. Experience in clinical supervision, providing evidence-based assessment and treatment for substance use and co-occurring mental health disorders. Experience with federally funded grants, research, program evaluation, or participation in clinical trials is preferred. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email: Caroline_Easton@urmc.rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179652": {
      "title": "Time as Reported CPEP Physician-3",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Psychiatry: Psychiatry: Crisis Services Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Department of Psychiatry, a department of the University of Rochester, is recruiting a physician for the Comprehensive Psychiatric Emergency Program (CPEP ).Join a vibrant, multidisciplinary team providing acute psychiatric care in an emergency setting.  This practice location is currently using the EPIC electronic medical records system and training will be provided. With over 10,000 visits per year, we are the primary provider of emergency psychiatric services to our diverse and vibrant community in Western New York. Our program has a 24/7 interdisciplinary team of psychiatrists, nurse practitioners, RN's and social workers, and encompasses a dedicated behavioral health space immediately adjacent to the Emergency Department, Extended Observation Beds unit, a Mobile Crisis Team, and currently expanding with a Crisis Stabilization Hub.One of the nation's top academic medical centers, the University of Rochester Medical Center forms the centerpiece of the University's health research, teaching, patient care and community outreach missions. The University's health care delivery network is anchored by Strong Memorial Hospital - an 800-bed, University-owned teaching hospital which boasts specialty programs that consistently rank among the best in the nation. At URMC, our robust teaching and research programs transform the patient experience with fresh ideas and approaches steeped in disciplined science. Here, care is delivered by health care professionals who innovate, take intelligent risks, and care deeply about the lives they touch. The Greater Rochester area and surrounding counties constitute a community of over one million residents spread over many neighborhoods and townships. With a wealth of unique attractions and events spanning all four seasons, the city has been rated by Forbes as one of America's top ten most livable cities, #3 Best Places to Raise a Family 2010, Top 50 Most Educated Cities in America, and boasts affordable housing and public schools that rank among the highest in the nation. Hourly rate dependent on day worked and shift worked. Requirements: Must Possess an MD or equivalent and be board certified (or board eligible) Must obtain NYS licensure prior to start Must be commiteed to working to be \"Ever Better\" while employing out ICARE values of integrity, compassion, accountability, respect, excellence Candidates applying to this position will be expected to secure an individual DEA and will be required to complete a post-offer health assessment and drug test at the University's Employee Health site in Rochester, NY at least one month prior to start. If interested in this position, please reach out to Sue DiGiovanni, MD directly to discuss this position, at: Sue_Digiovanni@urmc.rochester.edu If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187154": {
      "title": "Full-time Psychiatrist for CPEP Program",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Psychiatry: Psychiatry: Crisis Services Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Division of Adult Acute Psychiatry in the University of Rochester Department of Psychiatry invites applications for a full time psychiatrist with interest and/or experience in working with an acute patient population in an emergency psychiatry setting, the Comprehensive Psychiatric Emergency Program (CPEP). Join a vibrant, multidisciplinary team providing acute psychiatric care in CPEP. This is a unique opportunity to work as part of a collaborative interdisciplinary team together with psychiatrists, trainees, advanced practice providers, nursing staff, and clinical evaluators. The position would be sited at Strong Memorial Hospital at the University of Rochester Medical Center. This full time position includes an academic appointment with the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry at the rank of clinical senior instructor, clinical assistant or clinical associate professor, commensurate with experience and accomplishments. Teaching and clinical supervision of psychiatric residents and medical students is an integral part of this position. With over 9,000 visits per year, we are the primary provider of emergency psychiatric services to our diverse and vibrant community in Western New York. Our program has a 24/7 interdisciplinary team of psychiatrists, nurse practitioners, RN's and social workers, and encompasses a dedicated behavioral health space immediately adjacent to the Emergency Department, Extended Observation Beds unit, a Mobile Crisis Team, and currently expanding with a Crisis Stabilization Hub. One of the nation's top academic medical centers, the University of Rochester Medical Center forms the centerpiece of the University's health research, teaching, patient care and community outreach missions. The University's health care delivery network is anchored by Strong Memorial Hospital - an 800-bed, University-owned teaching hospital which boasts specialty programs that consistently rank among the best in the nation. At URMC, our robust teaching and research programs transform the patient experience with fresh ideas and approaches steeped in disciplined science. Here, care is delivered by health care professionals who innovate, take intelligent risks, and care deeply about the lives they touch. The Greater Rochester area and surrounding counties constitute a community of over one million residents spread over many neighborhoods and townships. The city is well regarded for a wealth of unique attractions and events spanning all four seasons, affordable housing, and public schools that rank among the highest in the nation. Total Compensation Range: Sr. Instructor $209,000 - $260,264 Assistant Professor $221,350 - $287,611 Associate Professor $243,200 - $315,271 Requirements: Must Possess an MD or equivalent and be board certified (or board eligible) Must obtain NYS licensure prior to start Must have an unrestrcited DEA Must be commiteed to working to be \"Ever Better\" while employing out ICARE values of integrity, compassion, accountability, respect, excellence Candidates applying to this position will be expected to secure an individual DEA and will be required to complete a post-offer health assessment and drug test at the University's Employee Health site in Rochester, NY at least one month prior to start. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, please email sue_digiovanni@urmc.rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position.  Individual salaries will be determined within the job's salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alingment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184232": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor (Supportive Care in Cancer)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Surgery: Surgery: Cancer Control Location: Saunders Research Building The Department of Surgery at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry is seeking a non-tenure track Research Assistant Professor for the NCI-supported T32 clinical and translational research training position in the Division of Supportive Care in Cancer.  The program eagerly seeks highly motivated early-career stage individuals with doctorates (PhD, Dr. P.H., M.D.) in health-related areas, including translational science, who are looking for skills training in cancer control research and grant writing towards developing a successful research career as an independent investigator.  NIH requires candidates must be US citizens or permanent residents.  Two years of funding with stipends are offered along with health insurance, tuition, research support and travel to up to four scientific meetings per year.  Applications for women and those from minority groups are strong encouraged.  Prior post-doctoral experience is allowed.  Doctoral degree requirements must be met prior to hire.  Post offer drug screen is required. Doctorate degree (PhD, Dr. P.H., M.D.)  NIH requires candidates must be US citizens or permanent residents.  Applications for women and those from minority groups are strongly encouraged.  Prior postdoctoral experience is allowed.  Doctoral degree requirements must be met prior to hire.  Post offer drug screen is required If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position.  If not, please create an Interfolio account.  For questions/concerns pertaining to this position, email Anne Hynes at anne_hynes@urmc.rochester.edu . The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191282": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Bassoon(tenure eligible)(30ESM-300106-WBP-FY27-1017)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: Academic Center: Eastman School of Music: Woodwinds, Brass, and Percussion Location: Eastman School Of Music The Eastman School of Music of the University of Rochester invites applications for a full-time faculty appointment in Bassoon beginning 1 July 2027. Rank and salary will be commensurate with experience. Responsibilities include teaching applied-music majors, teaching orchestral repertoire classes, andmaintaining national/international standing as a performing artist and teacher. The faculty member willcontribute to the musical life of the Eastman School of Music by participating in recruitment, auditions,juries, and recitals. In compliance with the NY Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $100,000 - $160,000. The University of Rochester considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, and internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. Candidates should have strong reputations as performers on the national and/or international level, in addition to a proven record of successful recruiting and teaching of outstanding tudents in a conservatory or university music school. Review of applications will begin on September 22, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. To receive full consideration, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, links to 3 recordings of performances and/ or teaching examples, and three confidential letters of recommendation. Additional materials may be requested at a later date . For Assistance please reach out mailbox: humanresources@esm.rochester.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191281": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Jazz Saxophone(tenure eligible)(30ESM-300108-JAZ-FY27-1015)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: Academic Center: Eastman School of Music: Jazz Studies & Contemporary Media Location: Eastman School Of Music The Eastman School of Music of the University of Rochester invites applications for a full-time faculty appointment in Jazz Saxophone beginning 1 July 2027. Rank and salary will be commensurate with experience. Responsibilities include teaching applied-music majors and maintaining national/international  standing as a performing artist and teacher. The faculty member will contribute to the musical life of the Eastman School of Music by participating in recruitment, auditions, juries, and recitals.In compliance with the NY Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $100,000 - $160,000. The University of Rochester considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, and internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. Candidates should have strong reputations as performers on the national and/or international level, in addition to a proven record of successful recruiting and teaching of outstanding students in a conservatory or university music school. Review of applications will begin on September 22, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. To receive full consideration, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, links to 3-6 recordings of performances and/ or teaching examples, and three confidential letters of recommendation. Additional materials may be requested at a later date. For assisatance with the application please reach out to mailbox humanresources@esm.rochester.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/178306": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Double Bass (Tenure Eligible)(30ESM-300102-STR-FY27-1016)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: Academic Center: Eastman School of Music: Strings, Harp, & Guitar Location: Eastman School Of Music The Eastman School of Music of the University of Rochester invites applications for a full-time faculty appointment in Double Bass beginning 1 July 2027. Rank and salary will be commensurate with experience. Responsibilities include teaching applied-music majors and maintaining national/international standing as a performing artist and teacher. The faculty member will contribute to the musical life of the Eastman School of Music by participating in recruitment, auditions, juries, and recitals. In compliance with the NY Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $85,000 - $150,000. The University of Rochester considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, and internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. Candidates should have strong reputations as performers on the national and/or international level, in addition to a proven record of successful recruiting and teaching of outstanding students in a conservatory or university music school. For assisatance with the application please reach out to mailbox humanresources@esm.rochester.edu Review of applications will begin on 9.22.26 and will continue until the position is filled. To receive full consideration, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, links to 3-6 recordings of performances and/ or teaching examples, and three confidential letters of recommendation. Additional materials may be requested at a later date."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187227": {
      "title": "Professor of Music Leadership (Open Rank) & Director, Institute for Music Leadership (30ESM-300081-IML-FY27-1014)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: Academic Center: Eastman School of Music: Institute for Music Leadership Location: Eastman School Of Music The Eastman School of Music invites applications and nominations for Director of the Institute for Music Leadership and Professor of Music Leadership. This faculty position includes a 50% administrative role. This is a multi-year, renewable, non-tenure eligible position. Entering its 30th year , the Institute for Music Leadership plays a central role in preparing musicians for sustainable, impactful careers. The faculty member in this role will provide strategic and artistic leadership for IML, oversee the Master’s program in Music Leadership , and support the development of innovative, industry‑connected and project‑based learning experiences that reflect today’s vibrant music profession. Responsibilities include: In partnership with the dean and other senior leaders, overseeing the academic and strategic direction of the Institute for Music Leadership Coordinate and lead the Master’s degree in Music Leadership Maintaining and building meaningful connections across a wide range of music industry sectors (nonprofit, commercial, creative industries, emerging fields) Leveraging industry relationships to support experiential learning, internships, and professional opportunities for students Teaching and mentoring students Collaborating on fundraising, community partnerships, and external engagement Eastman welcomes applicants whose expertise has been developed primarily through professional practice, leadership, and innovation within the music industry, alongside or in place of traditional academic pathways. Required Qualifications: Master’s degree required in music or a related field Significant professional experience as a musician, innovator, and educator Demonstrated leadership within artistic, educational, cultural, or music‑industry organizations, or leadership as an active independent artist. Strong communication, collaboration, and mentoring skills Application Materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy and leadership experience Three letters of recommendation Review of applications will begin June 22 and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169150": {
      "title": "Med-Peds Transitional Care Faculty Position (164058)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Transitional Care Medicine Location: 905 Culver Road The Department of Medicine, Division of Transitional Care Medicine is seeking an Internal Medicine-Pediatrics Physician to join its growing Division of Transitional Care Medicine. The Division of Transitional Care Medicine is dedicated to clinical, education and scholarly activities for the care of youth and adults with chronic conditions that originate in childhood ( i.e. “Transitional Care Medicine”) including autism spectrum disorder, and other intellectual and developmental disabilities (IDD), congenital heart disease, metabolic disorders, spina bifida, sickle cell disease and cystic fibrosis . Clinical care is provided in the outpatient setting at the Complex Care Center, an innovative interdisciplinary primary care setting. Inpatient care settings include adult inpatient medical care at Highland Hospital, intensive behavioral therapy at Golisano Children’s Hospital, and inpatient consultation at Strong Memorial Hospital. Educational activities of the Division include fellowship, residency and student activities across disciplines. The division also has robust grant activities and evolving research infrastructure. This physician will be an integral member of the UR team . M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Internal Medicine and Pediatrics Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188735": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Full Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Pharmacology & Physiology Location: S & GG Wing - SMD The Department of Pharmacology and Physiology at the University of Rochester invite applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Full Professor rank.  We seek a creative, enthusiastic scientist with clear potential to secure extramural funding for their research program (active extramural funding is required for candidates for Associate or Full Professor) who will synergize with the highly collaborative environment of the Department and the strategic initiatives of the Medical Center’s broader research community.  The Department, which has added ten tenure-track faculty members over the past several years, offers outstanding research and graduate training environments. Established research strengths in the department revolve around cell signaling in the context of physiology and disease and include: calcium signaling, G protein-coupled receptor pharmacology and signaling, ion channel structure/function, and mitochondrial biology. While applicants with research interests in all areas in pharmacology and physiology are encouraged to apply, applicants with research programs that bridge the above department strengths with current institutional strategic initiatives in neuroscience, RNA biology, immunotherapeutics, and cancer biology are of particular interest. The successful applicant will receive a highly competitive start-up package, generous laboratory space, and access to a wide range of state-of-the-art core facilities. The University of Rochester Medical Center, the School of Medicine and Dentistry, and the adjacent Schools of Arts, Sciences and Engineering are part of a private, world-class research university, providing excellent opportunities for highly diverse, cross-disciplinary interactions and collaborations. Include a cover letter addressed to Dr. Robert Dirksen, Lewis Pratt Ross Professor and Chair of Pharmacology and Physiology; curriculum vitae; 2–3-page description of research plans; teaching statement; 2-3 recent key publications; three references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis and should be received by December 1, 2026. PhD and/or MD degree or equivalent. At least two years of post-doctoral training If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Jennifer Brennan at Jennifer_Brennan@urmc.rochester.edu The referenced pay range re presents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/132879": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine - Clinical Cardiology, Southern Tier, NY (124552)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Cardiology Location: Olean, New York The Department of Medicine, Cardiology Division, is seeking a Faculty to provide clinical cardiology services at sites in the Southern Tier area, focusing on Olean, New York.  Duties include clinical cardiology consultations, teaching, research, and noninvasive testing studies interpretation including echocardiography, Holter Monitor, Stress Testing, and ECG. Board Certified or Board Eligible in Internal Medicine and Cardiovascular Disease Must obtain NYS Medical License prior to start date Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for a faculty appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Post offer drug screen and health assessment – required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. The referenced pay range represents the minimum and maximum annual salary for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range, and will be determined by considering factors including, but not limited to, market data, education, experience, qualifications, expertise of the individual, and internal equity considerations. Incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/137290": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Medicine (129322)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Cardiology Location: Rochester, N.Y. The Department of Medicine, Division of Cardiology is seeking a Non-invasive cardiologist with subspecialty training in Advanced Heart Failure and Transplantation.  The successful candidate will join a team of 7 Advanced Heart Failure Cardiologists in a busy academic medical center.  The University of Rochester receives referrals from across a broad region of New York State with state-of-the-art advanced imaging and intensive care unit facilities. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain New York State Medical License prior to employment start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Cardiovascular Disease and Advanced Heart Failure and Transplantation Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/137321": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor of Medicine (129356)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Cardiology Location: Rochester, NY The Department of Medicine, Division of Cardiology is seeking an Advanced Heart Failure and Transplantation (AHFT) cardiologist to join an elite team of academic physicians as our Medical Director of Heart Transplantation. The successful candidate will have expertise in Advanced Heart Failure with a focus on Cardiac Transplantation. The successful candidate will report directly to the Medical Director of Advanced Heart Failure and work closely with our Surgical Director of Heart Transplantation.  Interest and expertise in Adults with Congenital Heart Disease welcome. Non-Invasive Cardiologist with subspecialty training in Advanced Heart Failure and Transplantation. The successful candidate will join a team of 7 Advanced Heart Failure Cardiologists in a busy academic medical center.  The University of Rochester receives referrals from across a broad region of New York State with state-of-the-art advanced imaging and intensive care unit facilities. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain New York State Medical License prior to employment start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Cardiovascular Disease and Advanced Heart Failure and Transplantation Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/145702": {
      "title": "General Cardiologist for Geneva General (138474)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Cardiology Location: Geneva, NY The Department of Medicine, Division of Cardiology,  is seeking a full-time General Cardiologist to provide clinical services at sites in the Southern Tier area, with a focus primarily at Geneva General Hospital.  Duties include clinical cardiology consultations, teaching, clinical research, and noninvasive testing studies interpretation including echocardiography, Holter Monitor, and ECG readings. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Internal Medicine and Cardiovascular Disease Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/167117": {
      "title": "Director - Advanced Heart Failure Program (161770)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Cardiology Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Department of Medicine, Cardiology Division is seeking a nationally recognized leader in advanced heart failure and transplant cardiology to serve as Director of the Advanced Heart Failure Program, within the Division of Cardiology. This is a unique opportunity to lead and grow one of the most comprehensive advanced heart failure programs in the nation and make a meaningful impact on clinical care, research, and education. The successful candidate will join a collaborative, and highly accomplished academic team. As Director of Advanced Heart Failure, the appointee will work closely with our Surgical Directors of Heart Failure, Heart Transplantation and Mechanical Circulatory Support and with the Medical Directors of Heart Transplantation and Ventricular Assist Devices. Academic appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor is available, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Program Highlights: Heart Transplantation : ~20 transplants/year (over 375 total), including heart-kidney transplants, with ongoing innovation including DCD NRP protocols and heart preservation systems. LVAD Program : Among the largest in the U.S., with 65-85 implants/year and over 1,000 durable implants to date; with nearly 280 patients currently supported. Surgical Team : Three full-time cardiothoracic surgeons perform heart transplant and LVAD surgeries. Clinical Infrastructure : Includes 9.2 AHFT cardiologists, 12 outpatient APPs, dedicated transplant RNs, and robust QI, regulatory, and data management teams. Research Excellence : Strong support from the Clinical Cardiovascular Research Center , the Clinical & Translational Science Institute , and the Aab Cardiovascular Research Institute . Key Responsibilities: Lead a comprehensive advanced heart failure and transplant program in partnership with surgical, critical care, and multidisciplinary teams. Direct clinical operations across inpatient and outpatient settings, including heart transplantation and mechanical circulatory support (e.g., VADs). Oversee and enhance quality improvement initiatives, clinical protocols, and regulatory compliance. Expand and mentor a team of dedicated cardiologists and advanced practice providers. Grow the ACGME-accredited Advanced Heart Failure Fellowship program. Advance clinical, translational, or outcomes-based research. Support collaboration across specialties including congenital heart disease and pulmonary hypertension. Contribute to education and mentorship of trainees and medical students. Division and Facilities: The Division of Cardiology includes over 76 faculty members with expertise in general cardiology, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology, imaging, heart failure, cardio-oncology and more. The division supports four fellowship programs and is home to a new, dedicated 22-bed Cardiac ICU and a 23-bed Advanced Heart Failure Unit. A state-of-the-art cardiovascular tower is under construction and set to open in 2027. Living in Rochester: Rochester, NY is a vibrant, affordable city known for its cultural richness and natural beauty. It offers nationally ranked schools, renowned music and arts institutions (e.g., Eastman School of Music), and year-round recreational opportunities on Lake Ontario and in the Finger Lakes region. It holds a deep legacy in civil rights and women's suffrage history and offers a welcoming, family-friendly environment. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Cardiovascular Disease and Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant Cardiology Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188737": {
      "title": "Interventional Cardiologist (186417)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Cardiology Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The Cardiology Division of the University of Rochester Medical Center is recruiting a board certified/board eligible interventional cardiologist at the Assistant or Associate Professor level for its clinical interventional cardiology program. This program currently consists of a 7-member clinical faculty group with high volumes of diagnostic, interventional, and structural cardiac procedures serving a 7-hospital health system that provides care throughout upstate and western New York. Candidates with experience and interest in high-risk and complex PCI and mechanical circulatory support will be strongly considered as the medical center is a tertiary referral center supporting one of the largest VAD programs in the country and the only heart transplant program in western and upstate New York. Structural heart disease training is not required. The clinical program is complimented by a highly regarded cardiovascular clinical research program with substantial NIH and industry funding. A very competitive compensation and benefits package is offered. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Cardiovascular Disease and Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant Cardiology Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191268": {
      "title": "Advanced Heart Failure & Transplant Cardiologist (189419)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Cardiology Location: Strong Memorial Hospital Position Overview The Department of Medicine, Division of Cardiology at the University of Rochester Medical Center is seeking a board-eligible or board-certified Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant (AHFT) cardiologist to join our growing academic Advanced Heart Failure Program. The successful candidate will join an established team of 7 Advanced Heart Failure cardiologists and 3 cardiac transplant/mechanical circulatory support surgeons providing comprehensive care for patients with advanced heart failure, cardiogenic shock, heart transplantation, and mechanical circulatory support. We welcome applications from both recent graduates of an ACGME-accredited Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant Cardiology fellowship and experienced AHFT cardiologists. Academic appointment will be at the Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor level, commensurate with experience and qualifications. The Opportunity This position provides a broad academic practice in Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant Cardiology, including inpatient and outpatient advanced heart failure care, heart transplantation, durable and temporary mechanical circulatory support, cardiogenic shock, hemodynamic assessment, and multidisciplinary evaluation of patients for advanced therapies. Faculty participate in the dedicated Advanced Heart Failure inpatient service, outpatient Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant clinics, transplant and LVAD selection conferences, and teaching of cardiovascular disease fellows, residents, and medical students. Opportunities are available to develop focused clinical or academic interests in heart transplantation, LVAD/MCS, cardiogenic shock, pulmonary hypertension, cardio-oncology, adult congenital heart disease, clinical research, quality improvement, donor utilization, and transplant innovation. Protected academic time is available for teaching, research, quality improvement, and other scholarly activities based on the candidate's interests and career goals. Program Highlights · 7 dedicated Advanced Heart Failure cardiologists. · 3 cardiac surgeons performing heart transplantation and mechanical circulatory support procedures. · More than 400 heart transplants performed since program inception. · Established DCD heart transplantation program, including Normothermic Regional Perfusion (NRP). · Use of advanced heart preservation and transport technologies. · One of the largest durable LVAD programs in the region, with over 1,000 durable LVAD implantations. · Approximately 300 patients currently supported with durable LVADs. · Dedicated 22-bed Cardiac Intensive Care Unit staffed by cardiac critical care intensivists. · Dedicated Advanced Heart Failure inpatient service. · Comprehensive temporary MCS and cardiogenic shock capabilities. · Highly experienced multidisciplinary team of transplant and LVAD APPs, coordinators, pharmacists, social workers, dietitians, rehabilitation specialists, quality and regulatory professionals, and data specialists. Academic Environment The University of Rochester Medical Center is a major academic and quaternary referral center serving patients throughout Upstate and Western New York and beyond. The Division of Cardiology includes more than 70 cardiologists spanning advanced heart failure, transplantation, mechanical circulatory support, interventional cardiology, electrophysiology, structural heart disease, cardiovascular imaging, cardio-oncology, pulmonary vascular disease, preventive cardiology, and women's cardiovascular health. Faculty have opportunities for clinical, translational, and basic science research through the Clinical Cardiovascular Research Center, Clinical & Translational Science Institute, and Aab Cardiovascular Research Institute. The position offers opportunities for career development in clinical excellence, education, investigation, program development, and academic leadership. Mentorship will be provided for junior faculty and recent AHFT fellowship graduates. M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Cardiovascular Disease and Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant Cardiology Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194215": {
      "title": "Non-Invasive General Cardiologist with Advanced Echocardiography (192620)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Cardiology Location: Strong Memorial Hospital The University of Rochester Medical Center is seeking a board-certified or board-eligible cardiologist with advanced expertise in echocardiography and structural heart imaging. This position combines 0.5 FTE in cardiovascular imaging with 0.5 FTE in non-invasive general cardiology . Position Responsibilities Cardiovascular Imaging and Structural Heart Imaging – 0.5 FTE Interpret transthoracic and transesophageal echocardiograms, including complex and advanced studies. Perform and interpret three-dimensional echocardiography and other advanced echocardiographic imaging, as appropriate. Provide imaging support for the evaluation and longitudinal management of patients with structural and valvular heart disease. Participate in preprocedural planning and intraprocedural imaging for structural heart interventions, which may include: Transcatheter aortic valve replacement. Transcatheter mitral and tricuspid valve interventions. Left atrial appendage occlusion. Atrial septal defect and patent foramen ovale closure. Paravalvular leak assessment and closure. Collaborate closely with interventional cardiologists, cardiac surgeons, anesthesiologists, radiologists, sonographers, and other members of the multidisciplinary structural heart team. Participate in echocardiography laboratory quality assurance, protocol development, accreditation activities, and appropriate-use initiatives. Contribute to the education and supervision of cardiology fellows, residents, medical students, and echocardiography laboratory staff. Clinical Cardiology – 0.5 FTE Provide outpatient general or consultative cardiology care through regularly scheduled clinics. Evaluate and manage patients with cardiovascular disease, including hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, valvular heart disease, coronary artery disease, heart failure, arrhythmias, and cardiovascular risk factors. Provide approximately four weeks of inpatient cardiology service per year . Collaborate with primary care physicians, cardiovascular subspecialists, and other clinical teams to ensure coordinated, patient-centered care. Participate in divisional conferences, case reviews, and other clinical and educational activities. Academic Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to the academic mission of the University of Rochester Medical Center through teaching, mentorship, clinical scholarship, quality improvement, or research. Academic rank and appointment will be commensurate with the candidate’s experience and qualifications. Required Qualifications M.D. Degree or equivalent Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Eligible for Board Certification in Cardiovascular Disease Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements Advanced training and demonstrated expertise in echocardiography. Experience in transesophageal, three-dimensional, and structural heart imaging. Strong clinical judgment, communication skills, professionalism, and commitment to multidisciplinary care. Demonstrated interest in teaching and working in an academic medical center. Preferred Qualifications Additional fellowship training in advanced cardiovascular imaging or structural heart imaging. Experience providing intraprocedural imaging during structural heart interventions. Record of clinical research, educational scholarship, quality improvement, or program development. Board certification or eligibility in echocardiography through the National Board of Echocardiography is preferred. If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175454": {
      "title": "Faculty - Stem Cell Transplantation and Cellular Therapy (171124)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Hematology/Oncology Location: Strong Memorial Hospital THE POSITION The Department of Medicine, Division of Hematology Oncology is seeking a clinical researchers with a focus on contributing to a robust clinical trial portfolio supporting Wilmot Cancer Institute’s patient population and furthering scientific and clinical discovery. This will be achieved through a collaborative spirit of partnership with internal teams, including basic and translational scientists, clinicians and investigators, and other clinical and support staff.   The ideal candidate will be expected to be a trusted colleague, clinician, investigator, and leader, and build productive relationships with teams across Wilmot, URMC, and UR Medicine, faculty, staff, residents, and fellows.  Candidates will need to lead an active clinical practice, supporting clinical trial accruals and contributing to ongoing clinical and translational research, and ideally building relationships across the clinical and basic science departments, funded investigators, clinical trials office.  A competitive salary, generous benefits, and programmatic and research support will be provided. THE ENVIRONMENT Wilmot provides best-in-class cancer treatment and care to approximately three million people in New York State and conducts pivotal research with the goal of preventing and conquering cancer through innovations in science, patient care, education, and community outreach. Wilmot features an 87-bed flagship cancer center, 13 outpatient locations, and one of the state’s largest blood and marrow transplant programs. Wilmot is home to the region’s first cancer survivorship clinic and one of the nation’s first geriatric oncology clinics. Wilmot’s 198 oncology physicians and 514 oncology nurses see more than 7,000 new cancer patients each year. In 2024, Wilmot researchers had $30.9 million in cancer funding, $25.8 million in peer reviewed funding and over $14 million in NCI funding. URMC and UR Medicine (the clinical enterprise) form the centerpiece of the University’s medical research, teaching, patient care, and community missions. URMC has an integrated administrative structure, budget, and strategic plan. As one of the nation’s leading academic medical centers, URMC ranks among the top quarter of U.S. medical centers in federal research funding, has an overall revenue of approximately $6 billion, and houses the flagship hospital, Strong Memorial Hospital — an 886-bed quaternary care facility. In addition, URMC includes the School of Medicine and Dentistry, School of Nursing, the Golisano Children’s Hospital, Eastman Institute for Oral Health, Sovie Center for Advanced Practice Providers, UR Medical Faculty Group, and UR Medicine comprises seven additional community hospitals. M.D., M.D./PH.D. Degree or equivalent degree from an accredited institution Successfully completed an accredited fellowship program Possess ABIM Board Certification in an oncology specialty Possess academic credentials and accomplishments for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or higher at University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must obtain a New York State Medical License prior to start date Eligible for a Faculty Appointment at the University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must meet all credentialing requirements Post offer Drug Screen and Health Assessment required Compliance with University and New York State health requirements If you already have an Interfolio account, please sign in to apply to this position. If not, please create an Interfolio account. For questions/concerns pertaining to the position, email Linda_Marchionda@URMC.Rochester.edu The referenced pay range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the base range of compensation for this faculty position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job’s salary range and established based on (but not limited to) market data, experience and expertise of the individual, and with consideration to related position salaries. Alignment of clinical incentive-based compensation may also be applicable and will be discussed during the hiring process."
    },
