    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176499": {
      "title": "Faculty - Hem/Onc Regional (172303)",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Medicine and Dentistry: Medicine: Medicine: Hematology/Oncology Location: Wellsville, NY The Wilmot Cancer Institute, a newly designated National Cancer Institute (NCI) cancer center, at the University of Rochester Medical Center, is seeking Hematology/Oncology faculty to join our regional sites in Upstate NY/Southern Tier area. Enjoy working alongside UR faculty MD/DOs, APPs, and nursing staff. Closely collaborate with experts across the Wilmot Cancer Institute through tumor boards, educational sessions and clinical trial opportunities. Our positions are a blend of outpatient Hematology/Medical Oncology with infusion center coverage. THE POSITION Opportunity highlights: University of Rochester faculty appointment J1, H1-B and O1 Sponsorship available Competitive compensation and benefits package Working alongside supportive Hematology Oncology faculty in the region M-F days (8am-5pm) - shared call system The Upstate NY and Southern Tier areas are home to friendly and safe communities, low cost of living, and highly ranked colleges and universities. There is ample opportunity for outdoor activities that span all four seasons, including hiking, biking, water sports, exploring the nearby Enchanted Mountains region and Finger Lakes regions, as well as farmer markets, wineries, and breweries. Possess academic credentials and accomplishments for appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor or higher at University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry M.D., M.D./PH.D. Degree or equivalent degree from an accredited institution Successfully completed an accredited fellowship program and possess ABIM Board Certification in an oncology specialty Possess academic credentials and accomplishments for appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor or higher at University of Rochester School of Medicine and Dentistry Must obtain a New York S