    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191698": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor Obstetric Nursing",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Nursing and Health Sciences: SON Session Faculty Location: Helen Wood Hall Time-as-reported (TAR) The University of Rochester School of Nursing is seeking adjunct clinical instructors for the obstetric and mother-baby specialties. Candidates must have a bachelor’s degree in nursing, a RN license, and relevant practice experience. The School of Nursing offers nationally accredited baccalaureate, masters, and doctoral degree programs. The University of Rochester School of Nursing prepares nurses to meet the challenges of   health care in the twenty-first century.  Our philosophy centers around unification, education, research and scholarly productivity, practice, nursing, consumer, and health. Instructors use the resources of the School of Nursing to engage, inspire and elevate student learning. SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach groups of students in the school’s pre-licensure obstetric nursing courses in labs and/or clinical settings. Participate in required course-related meetings, program faculty meetings, and faculty committees as needed or selected. Assist in student clinical assessments and grading assignments. Serve as a resource/advisor/mentor for students. REQUIREMENTS: Bachelor’s degree in nursing Current NYS licensure Demonstrated record of clinical excellence Superior interpersonal skills required Post-offer health assessment required Complete all agency requirements for clinical faculty compliance and credentialing PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Masters degree and prior experience teaching in a baccalaureate program is strongly preferred. NOTE:  This document describes typical duties and responsibilities and is not intended to limit Associate Dean or Dean from assigning other work as required."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192838": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor – Laboratory Faculty",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Nursing and Health Sciences: SON Session Faculty Location: Helen Wood Hall The University of Rochester School of Nursing is seeking adjunct laboratory instructors for our pre-licensure nursing programs. This includes health assessment and medical-surgical nursing labs. Candidates must have a bachelor’s degree in nursing, a RN license, and relevant practice experience. The School of Nursing offers nationally accredited baccalaureate, masters, and doctoral degree programs. The University of Rochester School of Nursing prepares nurses to meet the challenges of health care in the twenty-first century.  Our philosophy centers around unification, education, research and scholarly productivity, practice, nursing, consumer, and health. Instructors use the resources of the School of Nursing to engage, inspire and elevate student learning. SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach groups of students in the school’s pre-licensure nursing programs in labs and/or clinical settings. Participate in required course-related meetings, program faculty meetings, and faculty committees as needed or selected. Assist in student clinical assessments and grading assignments. Serve as a resource/advisor/mentor for students. REQUIREMENTS: Bachelor’s degree in nursing Current NYS licensure Demonstrated record of clinical excellence Superior interpersonal skills required Post-offer health assessment required Complete all agency requirements for clinical faculty compliance and credentialing. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Masters degree and prior experience teaching in a baccalaureate program is strongly preferred."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192796": {
      "title": "Assistant to Associate Professor of Clinical Nursing CRNA",
      "description": "Department: University of Rochester: Office of the Provost: University of Rochester Medical Center: School of Nursing and Health Sciences: SON CRNA Faculty Location: Helen Wood Hall The University of Rochester School of Nursing is seeking a doctoral-prepared Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist for a full-time, 12-month clinical faculty position within the Nurse Anesthesia Program. The successful candidate will join the program during its development and implementation phase in preparation for the inaugural cohort beginning in May 2027. The position includes an anticipated effort allocation of 80% to the School of Nursing and 20% to clinical practice. The School of Nursing allocation will include teaching, student advisement, curriculum and program development, scholarship, service, accreditation activities, and other responsibilities consistent with the faculty role. The clinical allocation will support continued clinical competence and experiential qualification in contemporary nurse anesthesia practice. Candidates must hold current certification as a Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist and be eligible for registered professional nursing and nurse anesthesia in New York State. Candidates should demonstrate current clinical expertise in nurse anesthesia practice and experience or interest in professional nursing education, educational technology, curriculum development, simulation, student advisement, program development, and academic service. Candidates are expected to demonstrate a commitment to excellence in graduate nursing education, interdisciplinary collaboration, clinical practice, and scholarly activity. Rank and salary are commensurate with education and experience. Clinical faculty are eligible for promotion along the clinical faculty track. The School of Nursing offers nationally accredited baccalaureate, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. The University of Rochester School of Nursing prepares nurses to meet the challenges of health care in the twenty-first century. Our student population often begins at the undergraduate level and progresses sequentially to advanced levels of nursing education. Accordingly, faculty are expected to align their instructional approaches with the overarching curriculum and with the understanding that students learn from multiple faculty members and across multiple platforms of delivery. Faculty members use the resources of the School of Nursing to engage, inspire, and elevate student learning. The Unification Model directs nursing education, research, and practice. Unification is not only a philosophical approach but also an organizational structure that operationalizes the interdependence among education, research, and practice. Education empowers nurses with the knowledge, attitudes, and skills necessary for leadership in professional practice and research. Research develops nursing knowledge to strengthen education and promote evidence-based practice. Nursing practice promotes continued excellence through the generation of new research questions and enrichment of the educational experience. The ongoing interaction of education, research, and practice benefits patients and communities by supporting high-quality nursing care. Specific Responsibilities ·         Teach and evaluate graduate-level nurse anesthesia courses using didactic, simulation, clinical preparation, hybrid, and online instructional methods. ·         Develop and revise course materials, learning activities, and assessment strategies; evaluate student achievement and provide timely, constructive feedback. ·         Serve as an academic advisor and mentor to assigned students, maintain regular office hours, and participate in student progression and remediation processes as needed. ·         Serve as a reader and/or advisor for DNP scholarly projects and support students in the development, evaluation, and dissemination of doctoral scholarly work. ·         Contribute to curriculum development, simulation-based education, program evaluation, continuous quality improvement, and the preparation of accreditation materials and reports. ·         Participate in the planning and evaluation of clinical education, including review of student clinical experiences and progression, collaboration with clinical partners and preceptors, and clinical site visits as assigned. ·         Participate in student recruitment, admissions, orientation, retention, and graduation activities. ·         Engage in scholarly activity, professional development, faculty governance, committee work, and service consistent with the clinical faculty appointment and academic rank. ·         Maintain current clinical competence through the 20% clinical practice allocation and integrate contemporary evidence, professional standards, and clinical practice into teaching and advisement. ·         Maintain all required licenses, certifications, credentials, privileges, and clinical compliance requirements and perform other duties consistent with the faculty role and program needs. Appointment and Effort Allocation This is a full-time, 12-month clinical faculty appointment. The anticipated allocation of effort is: • 80% School of Nursing responsibilities, including teaching, student advisement, DNP scholarly project support, curriculum and program development, simulation, scholarship, service, and accreditation-related activities. • 20% clinical practice to maintain current clinical competence and experiential qualification in nurse anesthesia. Specific teaching, clinical, scholarship, service, and administrative assignments will be determined annually based on program needs, faculty expertise, the School of Nursing faculty workload model, and applicable appointment expectations. Requirements • Earned doctoral degree from an institutionally accredited college or university. • Graduation from a nurse anesthesia educational program accredited by the Council on Accreditation of Nurse Anesthesia Educational Programs or its predecessor. • Current certification or recertification as a Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist through the National Board of Certification and Recertification for Nurse Anesthetists. • Current unrestricted registered professional nursing license and eligibility to practice as a Nurse Anesthetist in New York State. • Demonstrated record of clinical excellence and current competence in nurse anesthesia practice. • Ability to teach, advise, mentor, and communicate effectively with graduate students at varying levels of academic and clinical development. • Ability to contribute to DNP scholarly projects as a reader and/or advisor. • Strong interpersonal, organizational, written, and verbal communication skills. • Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, students, clinical partners, and interdisciplinary teams. • Commitment to excellence in teaching, student development, clinical practice, scholarship, and service. • Post-offer health assessment required. • Completion and continued maintenance of all University, School of Nursing, and clinical agency requirements for faculty compliance, credentialing, and clinical practice. Preferred Qualifications • Prior teaching experience in nurse anesthesia, advanced practice nursing, graduate nursing, or another health professions education program. • Experience with online, hybrid, simulation-based, or technology-enhanced learning. • Familiarity with the standards and accreditation processes of the Council on Accreditation of Nurse Anesthesia Educational Programs. • Experience coordinating or evaluating clinical education. • Evidence of scholarly activity, including research, quality improvement, educational innovation, presentations, or publications. • Experience caring for diverse patient populations across a range of anesthesia practice settings. Note: This document describes typical duties and responsibilities and is not intended to limit the Associate Dean, Dean, or Nurse Anesthesia Program Director from assigning other work as required. The referenced pay range represents the full base range of pay for this position. Individual salaries will be determined within the job's salary range and established based on market data, experience, expertise of the individual, and internal equity considerations."
    }
  },
